update public.questions set explanation = $e$Standardise: Z = (8 − 10)/2 = −1, since σ = √4 = 2. Then P(X < 8) = Φ(−1) ≈ 0.1587. The 0.8413 option is P(X < 12) = Φ(1), which answers a different question about the upper tail.$e$ where id = '2d26017c-a99c-48eb-bc18-2b2bbb3e43dd';
update public.questions set explanation = $e$1 km = 1000 m, so 2.5 km = 2.5 × 1000 = 2500 m. Converting up a unit means a smaller number, and converting down means a larger one. 25 m and 250 m move the decimal point the wrong way, and 25 000 m multiplies by 10 instead of 1000.$e$ where id = '2d3e418c-6bd2-4cff-b825-f56c5262d2e6';
update public.questions set explanation = $e$The double-angle formula for tangent is tan 2A = 2 tan A / (1 − tan²A), derived from tan(A + B) with B = A. The denominator has a minus sign. The form 2 tan A / (1 + tan²A) is sin 2A, not tan 2A.$e$ where id = '2f1fc959-43b2-475a-9802-452f797a8756';
update public.questions set explanation = $e$For X ~ B(n, p), P(X = 0) = (1 − p)ⁿ. Here n = 6 and p = 0.25, so P(X = 0) = 0.75⁶ ≈ 0.178. The 0.0156 option does not match this formula, and 0.25 is p itself, not the probability of no successes.$e$ where id = '39eb56c2-6660-4e2f-8710-cbe21b065864';
